TBH, the biggest worry I have is the fact that until there are actual explo=
its available, we're just hoping that the tests we write are reasonable - i=
ts a game of chinese whispers, where we think we grok the information corre=
ctly, and completely - but we we're playing with a very partial deck.


I did already find a few test tools - and thanks - yours also suggests that=
 with the RancherOS release I made a few days ago, that we've done what we =
can (ok, so I actually delayed and didn't release the patched version I gle=
aned was the set - I was able to use 4.9.34 - as we're trying hard to be pu=
re upstream whenever possible)


IDK - I wouldn't call it "on a golden platter" - I'm trying to suggest that=
 the bigger players have a tonne more knowledge and experience than we newe=
r and smaller players do - but perhaps we can work out how the smaller dist=
ros can also get some early information and guidance - and perhaps that'll =
